===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*weh₁-}}
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:verray<ety:bor<fro:verai<ety:inh<la-eme:vērāgus<ety:der<la-cla:vērāx>>>>>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|verray}}, from {{der|en|fro|verai|t=true}}, from {{der|en|la-eme|vērāgus}}, from {{der|en|la-cla|vērāx}}, derived from {{m|la|vērus}}, from {{der|en|itc-pro|*wēros}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*weh₁ros}}.

Distantly cognate with {{cog|ang|wǣr|id=true|t=true}}. Over time displaced the use of a number of Germanic words or prefixes to convey the sense 'very' such as {{m|en|fele}}, {{m|ang|full-}}, {{m|ang|mæġen}}, {{m|enm|sore|id=very}}, {{m|ang|sin-}}, {{m|ang|swīþe}}, (partially) {{m|enm|wel}}.

